<title>USA: GM February U.S. vehicle sales off 7.1 pct.</title>
<headline>GM February U.S. vehicle sales off 7.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp</p>
<p>			Feb 1-28, 1997     Feb 1-29, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		203,859	   234,138	     -9.3</p>
<p> Total Truck	    152,265	   165,245	     -4.0</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	  356,124	   399,383	     -7.1</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-Feb 28, 1997 Jan 1-Feb 29, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		394,601	   417,619	     -3.6</p>
<p> Total Truck	    293,523	   316,722	     -5.5</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	  688,124	   734,341	     -4.4</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 24 in latest month vs 25, 50 for year to date vs 51 in year ago.  </p>
<p>NOTE: Total GM car sales include U.S. sales figures from Saab Automobile AB, which is 50 percent owned by GM and 50 percent owned by Sweden's AB Investor.</p>
</text>
